Mitsui Collective Program Manager

Title:
Program Manager
Reports to:
Founder & Executive Director
Location:
Cleveland, OH 
Position Type
: Part-time, contract;
Hybrid — remote and on-site work;

About Mitsui Collective:
Mitsui Collective cultivates pathways towards Jewish embodiment. Our vision is to fully activate thriving, resilient, healthy, and diverse communities that embody Jewish values of equity, justice, compassion, and belonging in all our ways of being.. We believe that every body deserves to be nourished, strengthened, and sustained.  

Mitsui Collective is structured around two organizational branches: 

Studio Mitsui focuses on community building and supporting individuals in transformative change through embodied practice. We offer in-person programs and classes for the Cleveland area and online classes and resources for an international audience. 

The Mitsui Institute for Jewish Embodiment works primarily with organizations and professionals across the Jewish landscape through speaking engagements, workshops and consulting, and field-building work such as research, curriculum development, and trainings. 

We are currently a fully remote team based primarily in Cleveland, OH. As we continue to implement our strategic plan, we are both carrying forward the momentum of our national work and deepening our local impact in Northeast Ohio. 

Description:
Mitsui Collective is seeking an experienced and dynamic Program Manager for a ten-month part-time contract role from Sept 2026 - June 2027 with possibility of extension. 

The program manager will primarily support two critical new grant-funded programs: The Nitzotz Jewish Embodiment Teaching Fellowship (national and local) ; and Abracadabra: School of Practical Magic (local/Cleveland-based). They will also contribute limited general support to our online and Cleveland-based Studio Mitsui programs, and Mitsui Institute for Jewish Embodiment programs and projects. 

Listed below are the essential roles and responsibilities for this position. Strong candidates for this role demonstrate readiness to build in a new sector; ability to contribute your voice, knowledge, experience, and strategies; an entrepreneurial mindset ready for experimentation; and a track-record of independent, proactive project management skills and capacity. 

Key Responsibilities:

Abracadabra: School of Practical Magic
( 10-15 hrs/wk ) 
Support development of content-development, logistics, execution, and evaluation of three seven-week prototype sessions between October 2026-July 2027; 
Serve as primary point of contact between program venues for rental, vendors, and other partners; 
Run point for purchase and use of supplies, rental space, and other logistical needs; 
Serve as primary point of contact for teaching and other program staff; 
Support community-facing communications and marketing, including communications with parents and community stakeholders; 
Assist with outreach & community support;
Support grant-related documentation, communications, evaluation, metrics, and related needs;

Nitzotz Jewish Embodiment Teaching Fellowship
( 3-5 hrs/wk ongoing; up to 40 hrs during training retreat weeks)
Manage program planning, communications, and logistics for two 3-4 day training retreats (October 2026, January 2027) including lodging, transportation, meals, use of program space, and secondary facilitation;  
Support biweekly online community of practice sessions through scheduling, communication, tech support, attendance tracking, and secondary facilitation;  
Support grant-related documentation, communications, evaluation, metrics, and related needs; 

General Program Support
(3-5 hrs/wk) 
Serve as primary point of contact for new program and membership inquiries;
Support development of content, logistics, and execution of in-house programs including but not limited to pop-up programs, holiday festivals, ongoing programs;
Support community-facing communications and outreach;
Support communications between program staff and external clients;

Additional Responsibilities
(2-4 hrs/wk as time and capacity permit)
Assist development and sharing of online content, marketing materials, and social media campaigns;
Support development and sharing of educational / program content and resources
Support leadership staff on client and membership contracts, invoicing, and related tasks;

Important Skills, Training, and Experience:

Bachelor’s degree or equivalent work experience;
2-4 years experience in program management, education, community organizing, event planning, and/or related fields; 
Proven track record of independent, proactive project management and execution.
Demonstrated experience with and/or ability to learn and apply skills and knowledge relating to the job responsibilities outlined above; 
Excellent organizational, leadership, and decision-making skills;
Proficient in working with GoogleSuite (docs, sheets, forms) and/or Microsoft Office Suite, Mailchimp, project management, and CRM platforms;
Set priorities, work independently, multi-task with regular interruptions, problem solve, delegate tasks as appropriate, and coordinate projects successfully;
Strong communication skills, both verbal and written;
Work effectively in both in-person and virtual environments;
Work efficiently across time zones — primarily across the US, and on occasion outside the US;

The ideal candidate will confidently demonstrate the ability to:
Work both independently and as part of a team;
Proactively support building communities of belonging; 
Commit to join and support the growing Jewish embodiment field nationally and presence of Jewish embodiment in the Northeast Ohio region; 
Value and co-create holistic professional environments that support and nourish a healthy workplace culture and community;
Share a professional commitment to antiracism and anti oppression work as complex, lifelong, and continuously unfolding practices that impact us on all levels of body and culture; 
Hold and treat Mitsui Collective’s work with intentionality, care, and discretion;
Work well in a nimble, relationship-driven culture that values creativity, iterative responsive design, and emergent strategy;
Thrive in a collaborative environment and maintain a caring growth mindset when sharing ideas and receiving constructive feedback;

Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply for jobs unless they meet every single qualification. We know that you may not have every skill listed above, and encourage applicants of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives to apply if you meet the large majority of required qualifications, are hard-working and self-starting, are ready to be on a nimble and collaborative team, and think you would be a fit for this role with Mitsui Collective! 

Compensation and Workplace

Compensation

$23,000-$28,000 total compensation, commensurate with skill and experience; 
Paid in monthly installments from September 2026 - June 2027; 

Anticipated Start Date
: September 14, 2026 

Schedule and Location 

Mitsui Collective is a hybrid work environment based in Cleveland, OH with ongoing weekly programs conducted at partnership locations in the Cleveland area, online programs hosted from a variety of locations, and day to day work conducted remotely. Candidates for this position should expect to travel throughout the Cleveland area for on-site work during scheduled programs and occasional meetings and other events. As an independent contractor they may otherwise work at locations of their choosing. 

As an independent contractor, you will set your own working hours, with the exception of scheduled programs, events, and meetings relevant to your responsibilities. 

Mitsui Collective operates during a generally typical Mon-Fri 9-5 workweek. While you are not required to work within these specific hours, timely communication and availability is essential to successful execution of this role and maintaining a collaborative work environment. 

Typical Working Conditions and Essential Physical Tasks 

This position will work inside an office environment, as well as indoor and outdoor venues on occasion. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by a contractor to successfully perform the essential functions of this role. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.

Regular sitting, standing, typing, and repetitive computer use. Occasional walking, standing, climbing, stooping, bending, pushing, pulling, lifting, kneeling, and twisting. Frequently communicates with others and must be able to exchange accurate information.  

TO APPLY: 

Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. 

To apply for this position, please complete the application form: https://chevremitsui.co/Program-Manager-Application  

_____

Mitsui Collective strives to center the diversity of insight, perspective, and experience brought by people from backgrounds typically underrepresented in Jewish communal and institutional life. Candidates from historically marginalized groups — including but not limited to People of Color (Black, Asian, Latinx, Indigenous, multiracial, etc), Jews of Color, Sephardi and Mizrahi Jews, lesbian, gay, bisexual, trans, and gender non-conforming people, and people with disabilities — are encouraged to apply. We also welcome applications from people of diverse religious, spiritual, and cultural backgrounds.

Questions? 

Contact info@mitsuicollective.org  

